Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='nopython', at=datetime(2026, 9, 8, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='There is no Python and there is one workspace; new application behaviour goes into app/', body="*Layout.* THERE IS NO PYTHON (2026-09-08, ARCHITECTURE §8.6) and THERE IS ONE WORKSPACE (2026-09-09, §8.8). `app/` is the application — `core` (meaning, pure), `io` (the interpreters), `cli` (the one binary, ORGANISED BY VERB: `cli/src/commands/<verb>.rs` owns that verb's clap types and work, `verb.rs` is the argument tree and a `match`, nothing is named for the stage it arrived in; `suzatary-dev`, built only under the `fixture` feature, is that tree plus `bench` and the e2e fixture's verbs). `web/` is the TypeScript frontend, `android/` the portal, `scripts/` the operator's shell, `nix/` the deployment; `events/`, `events-suzatary/` and `state.json` the stores; `instance.toml` and `mbsyncrc` the configuration; `tokens.typ` at root (the colour roles). Gone with the Python: `suzatary/`, `tests/`, `bin/`, `prodrome/py/`, `ty.toml`, `ruff.toml`, `pyproject.toml`. New application behaviour goes into `app/`; two applications that both work is the failure mode.", rationale='No Python since 2026-09-08 (ARCHITECTURE §8.6); one workspace since 2026-09-09 (§8.8).', supersedes=()))